# Dependency injection

## Design principle

**One DI style for the whole daemon.** Practice name and singleton law follow
[`python-services-rules`](https://github.com/drivestream-lab/python-services-rules)
`dependency-injection.mdc`:

- Collaborators are injected at construction.
- The **container owns singleton** lifetime for long-lived services — do **not**
  use `get_instance()` / `OnceLock` service-locator patterns on service types.
- **Settings / config bags** may use a separate once-loaded pattern and are not
  mixed into the same “service singleton” story without an ADR.

Rust crate choice (`inject`, custom, etc.) is foundation/ADR — not a second
competing DI mechanism in the same binary.

## Construct vs run

Construction is cheap and synchronous. Opening sockets, MQTT, and host handles
happens in an explicit **initialize / run** phase after the runtime is up —
same two-phase idea as python-services infra `initialize()`.

## Related rules

- **Lifecycle:** `process-lifecycle.mdc`
- **Fail fast:** `fail-fast.mdc`
